{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791898056,"nonce":"d/QGomzxCyt5UQ3HRke86AheAcs=","title":"InlineFlow leaves the remainder of a long word overflowing after its first split","message":"Reproducer: ChimpMonk editor/tests/ToastSnapshot.hx, run scripts/editor.sh --toast-snapshot with local Ash. A persistent Video saved toast has a long file path plus Preview and Close. CSS gives the body min-width:0 and the description overflow-wrap:anywhere, word-break:break-all and width:100%. The text column is 180px wide, but the second painted text run is 568px wide and overflows the toast. Snapshot and bounds checks fail on the current AshUI commit.\n\nIn InlineFlow.lines, splitting a long word fills the first line. The queued remainder cannot fit even one character in the remaining room. The code then ends the line and appends the entire remainder without retrying its split, so every long unbroken URL/path can overflow despite CSS.\n\nPrepared patch: /private/tmp/chimpmonk-ashui-toast-wrap.patch. When no character fits and the line is nonempty, requeue the item, end the line and continue. The existing empty-line progress fallback remains in place. Verified against an isolated AshUI source copy; sibling working tree unchanged pending handoff/spec.md §10 approval. Native snapshots and painted descendant bounds cover both themes, persistent notice text, Preview and Close. See /private/tmp/toast-wrap-shots and /private/tmp/toast-wrap-patched-shots for before/after.","files":null}]}